{"ts": "2026-09-21T00:45:00Z", "event": "issue", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 1, "task": "TASK-005", "message": "deviated from the plan's literal Tool::resolve() -> Resolution(owned Tool) design: implemented Resolved<'a>/EffectiveTool<'a> as borrows into the base Tool or its override instead. Avoids cloning and keeps graph::select() returning Vec<&Tool> unchanged, so every downstream consumer (engine, probe, doctor, upgrade) only needed a Platform parameter threaded in, not a full Vec<Tool> ownership rewrite. Same observable behavior; much smaller diff.", "detail": {}}
{"ts": "2026-09-21T00:46:00Z", "event": "issue", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 1, "task": "TASK-008", "message": "unsupported_finding() lives in core::doctor as a constructor, but the merge of unsupported findings into a command's output happens in cli/commands (unsupported_findings() calling it per-command) rather than inside doctor::diagnose() itself. diagnose() only takes the platform-filtered tools list and reports on those; the caller (doctor/apply commands) appends unsupported findings separately. Keeps diagnose() ignorant of graph::select, avoiding a core::doctor -> core::graph dependency.", "detail": {}}
{"ts": "2026-09-21T00:50:00Z", "event": "task_done", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 1, "task": "TASK-001..008", "message": "Platform enum + resolve()/admits() (platform.rs); PlatformOverride + Tool::resolve()/upgrade_spec_for() + validate() checks (manifest.rs); graph::select() filters unsupported tools before/at topo-order and returns Selected{tools,unsupported} (graph.rs); --platform global flag + Ctx.platform (cli/mod.rs, output.rs); tool.unsupported.<name> info finding (doctor.rs) wired through every CLI command (list/plan/install/update/doctor/apply), the exec::Executor trait (now takes install:&Install alongside tool:&Tool), probe::probe_tool/probe_all/spawn_streaming, engine::build_install_plan/build_upgrade_plan, and upgrade::check_one/check_all/spawn_streaming, all platform-aware. TUI (app.rs) always plans for Platform::host().", "detail": {}}
